# Local signed + notarized desktop build (macOS only).
#
# Copy this to `.env.signing` in the repo root (gitignored) and fill in your values.
# When present, `make desktop-build` produces the SAME Developer-ID-signed +
# notarized app that CI publishes — so you can install it locally and confirm the
# release path works. Absent ⇒ a plain ad-hoc build (the default, unchanged).
#
# No cert / password here: signing uses the Developer ID already in your login
# keychain. You only need the identity string + the App Store Connect API key for
# notarization. The same values back the GitHub release (variable + secrets).

# Public identity string — from: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"

# App Store Connect API key (notarization). Issuer + Key ID + path to the .p8 file.
APPLE_API_ISSUER=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
APPLE_API_KEY=XXXXXXXXXX
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH=/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
